<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90363" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσχάσκω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσέχᾰνον</span>: pf. in
			pres. sense <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προσκέχηνα</span>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>gape</i>, or <i>stare open-mouthed at</i> one, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μηδὲ . . χαμαιπετὲς βόαμα προσχάνῃς ἐμοί</span>
			<i>fall</i> not prostrate before me <i>with loud cries</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				920
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>gape eagerly at, be greedy for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ λεγομένῳ προσκεχηνέναι παιδικῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.42.7
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῷ εἴδει τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					11.3.5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.560
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
